  "steps": [
    "Actual runtime loads one Studio root with seven module records; a drama scene stays prose and a required missing 3D capability leaves the base editor assembled and editable.",
    "Project types/templates, World, build and export dialogs open through the real system-mounted controllers without starting an engine.",
    "The real media view obtains the optional export provider and prepares an original image export through HTTP while author source remains unchanged.",
    "Ordinary Save persists only the explicit drama draft, retaining BOM, CRLF, repeated speakers, and document inventory; no scene representation is generated automatically.",
    "A future schema is preserved as author data with a local invalid-profile diagnostic; source editing and exact ordinary Save continue without rewriting the manifest or creating a 2D/3D scene.",
    "The actual settings module switches Chinese, English and Japanese at 390 px; the dialog has no horizontal page overflow and preserves the author profile/draft."
  ],
